WEBVTT

00:02:02.870 --> 00:02:05.540
It's all right.

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:07.200
Please be informed...

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:12.210
This craft is about to enter the Planet Satyros orbital rim slowdown field.

00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:16.880
Afterward, we will descend the linear shaft, and 25 minutes from now,

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:19.880
at 13:11, we are scheduled to arrive at Caune Spaceport.

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:24.380
Please do not worry. Now that we've made it this far, we'll be okay.

00:02:54.850 --> 00:02:57.190
Yes, that's right.

00:02:57.190 --> 00:03:02.190
I'm terribly sorry. The ratification draft has been snatched.

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:04.920
It happened without any of us knowing.

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:11.140
Good grief. And I bet none of the other passengers on the shuttle

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:12.540
had anything to do with it <i>this</i> time either.

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:17.540
Watch what you say. However, the M.O. does indeed appear to be the same.

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:19.210
Same M.O., see?

00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:21.950
How can somebody steal something from a shuttle within an orbital elevator

00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:25.220
without leaving any evidence?

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:27.220
All told, this makes it the 18th case.

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:31.810
The 19th. We've got to catch this criminal fast.

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:41.170
We cannot do that.

00:03:41.170 --> 00:03:42.170
Why not?

00:03:42.170 --> 00:03:45.000
Satyros here is a planet of commerce.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:48.510
We pride ourselves on being one of the pivotal circulatory centers of the galaxy.

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:51.010
How many ships do you think come and go

00:03:51.010 --> 00:03:53.840
within one minute here at the Caune Spaceport alone?

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:55.870
There's no way we could stop...

00:03:56.850 --> 00:04:00.520
Not stop them, just check them. A boarding check.

00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:01.850
This would permit the afore-mentioned crimes to...

00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:03.850
It's the same thing.

00:04:03.850 --> 00:04:06.020
Even at the request of GOTT,

00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:07.860
we cannot do any more than we already are at present.

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:10.860
Eh? Uh... but still...

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:15.870
That will be fine. This is the reason we were sent, after all.

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:19.770
With the cooperation of every state, business, and vessel

00:04:19.770 --> 00:04:21.210
that make use of this spaceport,

00:04:21.210 --> 00:04:24.210
we had them furnish us with precise data.

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:28.610
Once the hard copy of this data has been transported to Planet Aineias,

00:04:28.610 --> 00:04:31.820
we will have it analyzed at GOTT headquarters.

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:35.150
Are you guys GOTT?

00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:37.820
ES members!

00:04:37.820 --> 00:04:40.830
I am Dextera, of GOTT.

00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:43.490
Likewise, I am Sinistra.

00:04:43.490 --> 00:04:47.500
With these two here, there's no need to worry about robberies or hacking.

00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:50.090
We will be putting this plan into action.

00:04:52.840 --> 00:04:55.470
We're grateful for your cooperation.

00:04:58.510 --> 00:05:02.850
Caune Delivery, this is UAS 0003.

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:09.520
Five minutes before start up engine for Aineias spot 205.

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:17.530
UAS 0003 cleared. Start up your engines and STC clearance.

00:05:17.530 --> 00:05:21.200
The ES members are on there? The ones we heard about?

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:26.540
Yeah. But this is a trap. If we were to just go waltzing up to them...

00:05:26.540 --> 00:05:30.060
...they'd round us all up, huh?

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:36.710
But still, these guys are carrying a full load of top secret data

00:05:36.710 --> 00:05:38.150
from the commercial ships, right?

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:41.210
It'd be a real pain to just let them slip away from us with that.

00:05:42.490 --> 00:05:45.320
Are you suggesting that we could get the jump on ES members?

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:48.490
Top secret data, eh?

00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:50.830
With ES members?

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:55.700
Yeah. This is a sticky problem. But still...

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:07.180
Okay, let's go check in, Miss Montague.

00:06:07.180 --> 00:06:09.180
Miss Montague!

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:10.850
Éclair Montague!

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:14.720
R- right! Excuse me, Miss Padushka.

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:18.680
Are you all right?

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:23.190
Our mission is an important one!

00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:27.000
The ES members, <i>Dextera-san</i> and <i>Sinistra-san</i> are decoys.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:31.140
We're the ones who are actually carrying the data!

00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:34.470
R- right! I think I understand.

00:06:34.470 --> 00:06:37.170
Geez, you're so unreliable!

00:06:37.810 --> 00:06:40.840
Even supposing you have been a receptionist up until now,

00:06:40.840 --> 00:06:43.810
you're still GOTT personnel, right?

00:06:43.810 --> 00:06:46.480
S- shape up!

00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:51.160
Um, Miss Padushka, are you all right yourself?

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:54.830
l- l- I am all right.

00:06:54.830 --> 00:07:00.160
I have, after all, served as an SO member for seven years, now.

00:07:00.160 --> 00:07:03.170
A- aside from that, Miss Montague,

00:07:03.170 --> 00:07:07.840
I am a <i>Mrs.</i>

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:12.510
Ah, is that your husband? He sure looks like a kind gentleman.

00:07:12.510 --> 00:07:16.180
He's the commander of the third detachment of C-Force.

00:07:16.180 --> 00:07:19.450
Gluck, watch over me, okay?

00:07:21.190 --> 00:07:24.860
Okay, Miss Montague, never mind that, let's check in!

00:07:24.860 --> 00:07:29.020
R- right, Mrs... Ms. Padushka.

00:07:29.860 --> 00:07:34.130
You're so young for me to be calling you Mrs... Is that okay?

00:07:34.130 --> 00:07:38.470
It doesn't matter what you call me. Come on, let's just check in.

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:41.370
<i>You</i> were the one who said not to call you "Miss," you know...

00:07:43.470 --> 00:07:45.810
I will take your baggage for you.

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:50.510
N- no, you see, this... this is a carry-on!

00:07:52.150 --> 00:07:54.450
Well then, if you'll excuse me,

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:57.820
I need to have you fill out this application and confirm the contents.

00:07:57.820 --> 00:07:58.490
Sure.

00:07:58.490 --> 00:08:02.490
Sorry, but lately, there has been an increase in strange incidents.

00:08:02.490 --> 00:08:04.830
Fill out this form, if you please.

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:06.160
Let's see...

00:08:06.160 --> 00:08:10.830
Excuse, me, but I'm in a hurry! Where do I get on BNL 3522?

00:08:10.830 --> 00:08:14.510
Flight 3522 is departing momentarily.

00:08:14.510 --> 00:08:17.170
Please go around to deck number A-82.

00:08:17.170 --> 00:08:18.800
Thanks.

00:08:30.850 --> 00:08:33.950
T- the case!

00:08:35.130 --> 00:08:37.130
Ms. Padushka?

00:08:37.130 --> 00:08:41.290
Miss Montague! I've done something terrible!

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:46.100
It's an old trick, but it's still effective.

00:08:46.100 --> 00:08:50.130
One of them draws attention away, while the other one takes possession.

00:08:56.810 --> 00:08:58.820
Thank you, Miss Montague!

00:08:58.820 --> 00:09:03.820
Could you call me Éclair? I'd be more happy that way.

00:09:03.820 --> 00:09:06.160
Thank you, Éclair.

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:07.830
Ahem...

00:09:07.830 --> 00:09:09.830
Your baggage request.

00:09:09.830 --> 00:09:11.830
Oh yeah, that's right.

00:09:11.830 --> 00:09:15.170
Excuse me, I have this as well.

00:09:15.170 --> 00:09:17.500
You'll be taking some cargo as well, then?

00:09:17.500 --> 00:09:19.170
Yes, if you'd be so kind.

00:09:19.170 --> 00:09:21.510
I will get you a claim check.

00:09:21.510 --> 00:09:28.850
Caune Delivery, this is BOL 3600. Five minutes before start up engine...

00:09:28.850 --> 00:09:32.280
...for Aineias spot 224.

00:09:37.790 --> 00:09:39.460
Madam, your luggage?

00:09:39.460 --> 00:09:43.920
I beg your pardon, but my husband told me not to let go of my suitcase!

00:09:49.470 --> 00:09:51.800
Looks like they're finally departing.

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:54.140
Are you sure they're okay without us escorting them?

00:09:54.140 --> 00:09:58.440
Are you concerned for Éclair? If that's the case, then be my guest.

00:09:58.440 --> 00:10:01.100
I still have my job to do.

00:10:29.170 --> 00:10:33.110
You really are leaving her. That's pretty cold of you, isn't it?

00:10:33.110 --> 00:10:36.110
I don't like clingy relationships.

00:10:36.110 --> 00:10:38.240
Is that because breaking up is painful?

00:10:39.780 --> 00:10:42.620
Oh? Did I hit the mark?

00:10:48.130 --> 00:10:51.460
Our craft is currently advancing to the orbital rim.

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:54.030
After 23 minutes of circular acceleration,

00:10:54.030 --> 00:10:55.860
we will be heading to the warp gate.

00:11:05.710 --> 00:11:10.110
We please ask that you continue to keep your seatbelts fastened.

00:11:11.820 --> 00:11:13.150
Huh? Still not yet?

00:11:13.150 --> 00:11:15.490
Now, now, be quiet.

00:11:15.490 --> 00:11:19.090
It looks like everything has gone smoothly so far, huh?

00:11:19.090 --> 00:11:20.160
My goodness, I'm sweating here!

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:22.490
You're pretty tense, huh?

00:11:22.490 --> 00:11:27.830
Yes. I envy you, being so composed. I wonder if it's your youth.

00:11:27.830 --> 00:11:30.170
Not at all! Ms. Padushka, you're still...

00:11:30.170 --> 00:11:32.170
It's all right.

00:11:32.170 --> 00:11:38.130
The truth is, this is the first job this big that has been entrusted to me.

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:41.850
And it will probably be the last one.

00:11:41.850 --> 00:11:42.850
The last one?

00:11:42.850 --> 00:11:45.520
Mm-hmm. I talked it over with Gluck...

00:11:45.520 --> 00:11:49.850
...that's my husband, and that's what we decided.

00:11:49.850 --> 00:11:54.860
After this last job, I intend to resign from GOTT.

00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:56.720
But why?

00:11:59.860 --> 00:12:01.870
Congratulations!

00:12:01.870 --> 00:12:06.500
So you see, I have to make sure that this mission succeeds without incident...

00:12:06.500 --> 00:12:07.600
What?

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:12.210
A high frequency?

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:16.510
There's sleeping gas as well! A robbery? Done in this way?

00:13:00.190 --> 00:13:04.590
They've got us. Our movements have been discovered by the criminals.

00:13:12.200 --> 00:13:15.870
Shtay back, Éclair!

00:13:15.870 --> 00:13:20.540
You guysh are the orbital elevator robbersh, aren't you!?

00:13:20.540 --> 00:13:23.210
Ash long ash I'm shtill here,

00:13:23.210 --> 00:13:27.780
I won't allow you to lay a hand on thish girl, or thish cashe!

00:13:33.160 --> 00:13:36.160
H- hold on, now!

00:13:36.160 --> 00:13:37.160
Um...

00:13:37.160 --> 00:13:40.100
Nanomist Shield, expand!

00:13:45.170 --> 00:13:48.900
I won't let you come any closher!

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:07.260
R- retreat!

00:14:10.860 --> 00:14:13.200
Now, surrender quietly!

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:16.960
It's okay! We're okay now, Ms. Padushka!

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:20.200
Where are the criminals?

00:14:20.200 --> 00:14:23.870
They left, probably because they couldn't get through the shield.

00:14:23.870 --> 00:14:29.210
We're saved! I didn't possibly think they would be coming after us.

00:14:29.210 --> 00:14:32.180
Still, there's no way the pilot could not be aware

00:14:32.180 --> 00:14:34.480
of gas being mixed in with the air conditioning.

00:14:34.480 --> 00:14:36.150
Then, the pilot is in league with them?

00:14:36.150 --> 00:14:37.310
Probably.

00:14:40.490 --> 00:14:44.490
Éclair, you had the gas neutralized by the nanomist too, right?

00:14:44.490 --> 00:14:46.160
Y- yes.

00:14:46.160 --> 00:14:49.500
Come with me! We're taking him into custody!

00:14:49.500 --> 00:14:50.500
What's the matter?

00:14:50.500 --> 00:14:53.060
R- right, Ms. Padushka!

00:14:56.510 --> 00:14:57.730
Dammit!

00:15:00.180 --> 00:15:01.850
Nicely done!

00:15:01.850 --> 00:15:05.750
This is the first time I've ever used this equipment. It sure works well, huh?

00:15:12.190 --> 00:15:13.860
W- what is it!?

00:15:13.860 --> 00:15:17.950
Ms. Padushka, the control stick! Take the control stick!

00:15:24.530 --> 00:15:27.870
Mayday, mayday! This is BOL 3600!

00:15:27.870 --> 00:15:30.370
We've been caught up in the serial robbery incidents!

00:15:30.370 --> 00:15:31.480
Our present condition is deteriorating!

00:15:31.480 --> 00:15:36.150
What's worse, the regular pilot is an accomplice, so he is in custody!

00:15:36.150 --> 00:15:40.150
Presently, the Al and myself, one of the passengers, is piloting!

00:15:40.150 --> 00:15:42.880
Mayday, mayday, someone please respond!

00:15:44.150 --> 00:15:49.160
Éclair, when you're done there... huh? Éclair?

00:15:49.160 --> 00:15:52.290
Where did you go!? And at a time like this!

00:16:03.170 --> 00:16:05.140
Ta da~a!

00:16:09.850 --> 00:16:14.080
Those armaments! You mean the orbital police themselves are the robbers!?

00:16:14.080 --> 00:16:16.380
There's no redeeming these guys!

00:16:22.190 --> 00:16:24.530
Éclair! Is that where you went?

00:16:24.530 --> 00:16:26.200
Ms. Padushka?

00:16:26.200 --> 00:16:28.390
Don't move from there!

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:37.270
Those women!

00:16:40.480 --> 00:16:43.240
Ms. Padushka, nice!

00:16:52.160 --> 00:16:54.680
You're kidding! New troops?

00:17:02.170 --> 00:17:04.830
What? The helm's not working any more!

00:17:04.830 --> 00:17:06.970
Now that they've discovered who we are,

00:17:06.970 --> 00:17:08.840
we'll have to stage an accident and eliminate them!

00:17:08.840 --> 00:17:10.510
Find a suitable location and ram into them!

00:17:10.510 --> 00:17:12.510
Understood!

00:17:12.510 --> 00:17:13.980
For crying out loud,

00:17:13.980 --> 00:17:16.850
they've sent three wolves after a delicate little girl like me!

00:17:16.850 --> 00:17:19.680
It's just about time for your entrance. Could you wake up for me?

00:17:24.520 --> 00:17:27.390
We can't go that way, I tell you!

00:17:33.460 --> 00:17:34.790
What?

00:17:41.140 --> 00:17:43.700
Here we go, Donnerschlag!

00:17:51.150 --> 00:17:53.050
It's fixed!

00:18:10.830 --> 00:18:12.730
Round 2!

00:18:19.510 --> 00:18:21.600
You rotten little girl!

00:18:23.180 --> 00:18:25.550
All right, you're mine!

00:18:26.180 --> 00:18:27.620
Oh, no!

00:18:31.450 --> 00:18:33.390
Donnerschlag!

00:18:37.130 --> 00:18:39.290
N- now hold on!

00:18:43.130 --> 00:18:45.230
Just a little bit more now...

00:18:47.140 --> 00:18:49.300
Sure enough!

00:18:50.470 --> 00:18:51.940
Die!!

00:18:58.480 --> 00:18:59.880
What?

00:19:01.150 --> 00:19:05.160
Sorry. It's not our inclination to make a lady wait.

00:19:05.160 --> 00:19:06.820
Perhaps we were a little late?

00:19:06.820 --> 00:19:09.160
Mm-mm, that was good timing!

00:19:09.160 --> 00:19:10.830
That's good.

00:19:10.830 --> 00:19:15.030
Right about now, their group's base should also be under raid.

00:19:25.180 --> 00:19:29.850
As it turns out, the main criminals were just one segment of the orbital police.

00:19:29.850 --> 00:19:32.450
In addition to the way in which they attacked you,

00:19:32.450 --> 00:19:34.780
it seems they also employed a number of other methods,

00:19:34.780 --> 00:19:37.690
including cybersimulations, secret substitutions,

00:19:37.690 --> 00:19:40.320
and re-writing acceleration and deceleration diagrams.

00:19:41.120 --> 00:19:41.890
What's more,

00:19:41.890 --> 00:19:45.130
there were cases where the victims had been the clients themselves...

00:19:45.130 --> 00:19:47.800
double-bookkeeping insurance fraud.

00:19:47.800 --> 00:19:50.600
Well, everyone had their own motives,

00:19:50.600 --> 00:19:52.470
but that doesn't change the fact that it was criminal.

00:19:52.470 --> 00:19:54.470
Thank you very much!

00:19:54.470 --> 00:19:58.810
If you two hadn't been there, I don't know what would have become of us!

00:19:58.810 --> 00:19:59.980
Not at all.

00:19:59.980 --> 00:20:01.980
It's thanks to you two being so conspicuous

00:20:01.980 --> 00:20:04.150
that we were able to arrest the whole gang, after all.

00:20:04.150 --> 00:20:06.310
We're the ones who should be thanking you.

00:20:06.820 --> 00:20:11.490
Then, you mean, we were the ones who were the decoys?

00:20:11.490 --> 00:20:14.290
Whether you call yourselves decoys or bait,

00:20:14.290 --> 00:20:17.160
it was an old trick, but it's still effective.

00:20:17.160 --> 00:20:18.860
Really?

00:20:18.860 --> 00:20:23.830
Oh, oh no, the reaction to all that stress is just now kicking in...

00:20:23.830 --> 00:20:28.270
Ms. Padushka!? Ms. Padushka!?

00:20:32.440 --> 00:20:36.450
Thank you, everyone! Thank you very much, Chief.

00:20:36.450 --> 00:20:39.750
No, we're the ones who are grateful!

00:20:39.750 --> 00:20:42.790
I mean, for you to make such a big arrest on your last assignment!

00:20:42.790 --> 00:20:46.790
If you get the notion, you can come back any time you like!

00:20:46.790 --> 00:20:51.120
Thank you very much. I believe it is thanks to all of you.

00:20:55.470 --> 00:20:59.800
Thanks. It's because of you that I was able to carry out my last job.

00:20:59.800 --> 00:21:01.810
- Not at all! - But you know,

00:21:01.810 --> 00:21:06.140
a girl younger than marrying age such as yourself shouldn't be quite so reckless!

00:21:06.140 --> 00:21:09.110
You should be more elegant, okay?

00:21:11.150 --> 00:21:15.520
Still, knowing you, becoming an ES member could be more than just a dream!

00:21:15.520 --> 00:21:16.780
See you.

00:23:06.880 --> 00:23:08.410
<i>The day of the contract.</i>

00:23:08.410 --> 00:23:11.550
<i>Barriers that must be overcome stand squarely in the way.</i>

00:23:11.550 --> 00:23:13.890
<i>Do you leap over them? Do you avoid them?</i>

00:23:13.890 --> 00:23:16.220
<i>Or do you break them down?</i>

00:23:16.220 --> 00:23:20.720
<i>Next time on Kiddy Grade</i>
